@startuml
title ParametricCAD — Move/Rotate interaction

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor User
participant CadViewer as Viewer
participant SelectionState as Selection
participant TransformGizmo as Gizmo
participant TransformMath as Math
participant SnapManager as Snap
participant ModelingController as Controller
participant QUndoStack as Stack
participant TransformFeatureCommand as Command
participant Body

User -> Viewer : activate Move / Rotate
User -> Viewer : select feature A (tree or viewport)
Viewer -> Selection : normalize committed selection
Selection --> Viewer : primary = A
Viewer -> Gizmo : show at A bounding-box center
User -> Viewer : press axis or rotation ring
Viewer -> Viewer : capture primary A and original placement
Viewer -> Snap : collect source references for A

alt selection changes during an active transform
    User -> Viewer : select feature B
    Viewer -> Viewer : cancel active drag
    Viewer -> Selection : normalize committed selection
    Selection --> Viewer : primary = B
    Viewer -> Gizmo : detach A and show at B
end

loop mouse move
    User -> Viewer : move cursor
    Viewer -> Math : build camera ray and calculate delta
    Math --> Viewer : world translation / rotation
    Viewer -> Snap : evaluate candidates for source A
    Snap --> Viewer : best candidate with hysteresis
    Viewer -> Gizmo : highlight handle / snap target
    Viewer -> Viewer : update temporary AIS preview from original transform
end

alt release
    Viewer -> Controller : commitTransform(featureId, before, after)
    Controller -> Stack : push(command)
    Stack -> Command : redo()
    Command -> Body : resolve ID, set placement, recompute
else Esc
    Viewer -> Viewer : restore original AIS shape
end

note over Math
  Screen coordinates are converted to camera rays.
  Translation uses axis projection; rotation uses
  a pivot plane. No pixel-to-model coefficient.
end note

@enduml
